<title>JAPAN: G7 forex accord has filtered thru to markets -- MOF.</title>
<headline>G7 forex accord has filtered thru to markets -- MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The currency agreement reached in late April by the Group of Seven (G7) nations has now filtered through to foreign exchange markets, Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Our basic stance is to deal with excessive currency movements while carefully monitoring currency movements,&quot; he told the finance committee of the Upper House of parliament.</p>
</text>
